2026-10-08  Daniel Boyd  <danieljboyd@icloud.com>

	Window tabbing: dragging tabs and scrolling the bar, as libadwaita's
	AdwTabBar does.

	* Source/GSWindowTabBarView.m ([GSWindowTabBarView
	-trackTabAtIndex:fromPoint:]): New: a press on a tab dragged past
	GTK's drag threshold (8 points) moves it along the bar; Escape
	cancels; 32 points above or below the bar it is pulled out, and on
	the release joins the tabs of a window with the same tabbing
	identifier under the pointer or becomes a window of its own.  A
	tracking loop, with periodic events while a tab is dragged.
	([GSWindowTabBarView -autoscrollForDraggedTabAt:]): New: a tab held
	past an end of a bar whose tabs don't fit scrolls it.
	([GSWindowTabBarView -dropGapSlot],
	[GSWindowTabBarView -setDropGapSlot:]): New: the gap opened in a bar
	where a tab pulled out of another would drop.
	([GSWindowTabBarView -showDropGapAtScreenPoint:inBar:]): New.
	([GSWindowTabBarView -scrollOffset],
	[GSWindowTabBarView -setScrollOffset:],
	[GSWindowTabBarView -scrollWheel:]): New: tabs that don't fit at
	their minimum width scroll, a wheel step as GTK's (the visible width
	to the power 2/3); the selected tab is kept in sight.
	([GSWindowTabBarView -drawScrollFades]): New.
	* Source/GSWindowTabBarLayout.m (GSWindowTabSlot,
	GSWindowTabSlotAtOffset, GSWindowTabScrollToShow): New.
	* Headers/GSWindowTabbing.h (GSWindowTabDragged): New state bit.
	([GSTheme -windowTabBarScrollFadeWidthForWindow:],
	[GSTheme -drawWindowTabBarScrollFadeInRect:edge:window:]): Declare.
	* Source/GSWindowTabbingTheme.m: Their defaults.
	* Source/GSWindowTabbingWindow.m ([NSWindow
	-_tabbingMoveToNewWindowAt:], [NSWindow -_canBeTabbedWith:]): New,
	shared with -moveTabToNewWindow: and automatic tabbing.
	* Tests/gui/NSWindow/tabbing_drag.m: New.
	* Tests/gui/NSWindowTabGroup/group.m: Reordering, dropping, slots and
	scrolling.
	* README.md: Document them.

2026-10-08  Daniel Boyd  <danieljboyd@icloud.com>

	* Headers/GSWindowTabbing.h: GSWT_EXPORT, empty of dllimport, for the
	public functions and constant, in place of GS_EXPORT: the code is
	compiled into the theme or app that uses it, and GS_EXPORT made
	Windows builds warn (dllimport, LNK4217).  In libs-gui these become
	APPKIT_EXPORT.

2026-10-08  Daniel Boyd  <danieljboyd@icloud.com>

	Window tabbing: Apple's NSWindow tabbing API, drawn by GSTheme.
	(Draft for libs-gui: the paths are where each part goes there;
	README.md maps them to this repository's files.)

	* Headers/AppKit/NSWindowTab.h,
	* Headers/AppKit/NSWindowTabGroup.h: New files.
	* Headers/AppKit/AppKit.h: Import them.
	* Headers/AppKit/NSWindow.h (NSWindowTabbingMode,
	NSWindowUserTabbingPreference): New enums.
	([NSWindow +allowsAutomaticWindowTabbing],
	[NSWindow +setAllowsAutomaticWindowTabbing:],
	[NSWindow +userTabbingPreference], [NSWindow -tabbingMode],
	[NSWindow -setTabbingMode:], [NSWindow -tabbingIdentifier],
	[NSWindow -setTabbingIdentifier:], [NSWindow -tabbedWindows],
	[NSWindow -tab], [NSWindow -tabGroup],
	[NSWindow -addTabbedWindow:ordered:], [NSWindow -selectNextTab:],
	[NSWindow -selectPreviousTab:], [NSWindow -moveTabToNewWindow:],
	[NSWindow -mergeAllWindows:], [NSWindow -toggleTabBar:]): Declare.
	([NSResponder -newWindowForTab:]): Declare.
	(GSWindowTabBarDidChangeNotification): New notification.
	(GS_HAS_WINDOW_TABBING): Define.
	* Headers/Additions/GNUstepGUI/GSTheme.h (GSWindowTabState,
	GSWindowTabBarPlacement): New types.
	([GSTheme -windowTabBarHeightForWindow:],
	[GSTheme -windowTabBarPlacementForWindow:],
	[GSTheme -windowTabMinimumWidthForWindow:],
	[GSTheme -windowTabMaximumWidthForWindow:],
	[GSTheme -windowTabNewTabButtonWidthForWindow:],
	[GSTheme -windowTabBarMarginForWindow:],
	[GSTheme -windowTabSpacingForWindow:],
	[GSTheme -windowTabCloseButtonRectForTabRect:state:window:],
	[GSTheme -drawWindowTabBarBackgroundInRect:window:],
	[GSTheme -drawWindowTab:inRect:state:window:],
	[GSTheme -drawWindowTabCloseButtonInRect:state:window:],
	[GSTheme -drawWindowTabNewTabButtonInRect:state:window:]): Declare.
	(GSWindowTabBarViewForWindow, GSWindowTabFittedTitle): Declare.
	* Source/NSWindowTab.m,
	* Source/NSWindowTabGroup.m: New files, the model.
	* Source/GSWindowTabBarView.h,
	* Source/GSWindowTabBarView.m: New files, the tab bar: layout, hit
	testing, the close and "+" buttons, hover and tool tips.
	* Source/GSWindowTabbingPrivate.h: New file.
	* Source/GSThemeWindowTabs.m: New file, GSTheme's default tab bar.
	* Source/GNUmakefile: Add the new files.
	* Source/NSWindow.m: Implement the tabbing API.
	([NSWindow -orderWindow:relativeTo:]): A hidden tab ordered in is
	selected; a window ordered in for the first time may join the key
	window's group.
	([NSWindow -setTitle:], [NSWindow -setTitleWithRepresentedFilename:],
	[NSWindow -setDocumentEdited:]): Update the window's tab.
	([NSWindow -performKeyEquivalent:], [NSWindow -sendEvent:]): Take
	Ctrl+Tab, Ctrl+Shift+Tab, Ctrl+Page Up and Ctrl+Page Down while the
	window has more than one tab.
	([NSWindow -close]): Leave the window's group, showing the next tab
	first.
	([NSWindow -validateUserInterfaceItem:]): Validate the tab actions.
	([NSWindow -dealloc]): Release the tabbing state.
	* Source/GSWindowDecorationView.m ([GSWindowDecorationView -layout]):
	Lay out the tab bar.
	([GSWindowDecorationView -contentRectForFrameRect:styleMask:],
	[GSWindowDecorationView -frameRectForContentRect:styleMask:]):
	Reserve the tab bar's row.
